1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:02,375
[NARRATOR] <i>Claude Sirius,</i>

2
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:04,375
<i>one of only ten people</i>
<i>in the world</i>

3
00:00:04,459 --> 00:00:07,000
<i>to bear the title of</i>
<i>First-Class Magician.</i>

4
00:00:07,542 --> 00:00:09,501
<i>His magic is said to be</i>
<i>powerful enough</i>

5
00:00:09,584 --> 00:00:11,167
<i>to move the stars.</i>

6
00:00:11,834 --> 00:00:14,626
<i>He made history at 17 as</i>
<i>the youngest professor</i>

7
00:00:14,709 --> 00:00:17,083
<i>ever assigned to</i>
<i>the Royal Magic Academy.</i>

8
00:00:17,417 --> 00:00:19,542
<i>He was a charming young man</i>
<i>who helped train</i>

9
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:21,626
<i>the next generation</i>
<i>of magicians.</i>

10
00:00:21,834 --> 00:00:25,918
<i>However, after that,</i>
<i>he mysteriously vanished.</i>

11
00:00:28,209 --> 00:00:30,584
[deep breath]

12
00:00:31,918 --> 00:00:34,459
[ARIA] Hey!
Are you serious about flying?!

13
00:00:34,792 --> 00:00:37,417
Falling from way up there
wouldn't be a pretty sight!

14
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:39,125
Stand back and watch me.

15
00:00:40,792 --> 00:00:42,501
[SPICA] Air, grant me strength.

16
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:46,167
Grant me freedom.
Let the soaring winds take me.

17
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:48,334
Release me from
my shackles to the land.

18
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:50,375
My staff...

19
00:00:51,417 --> 00:00:52,250
[giggles]

20
00:00:53,375 --> 00:00:55,918
-[SPICA] Fly!
-[♪ whimsical music]

21
00:00:59,959 --> 00:01:02,125
[screams]

22
00:01:09,459 --> 00:01:12,083
[Aria laughs] See?

23
00:01:12,167 --> 00:01:14,042
I told you you'd crash again,
you dork!

24
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:15,834
Oh, Spica.
I don't think I could ever

25
00:01:15,918 --> 00:01:17,667
get tired of watching you
try to fly.

26
00:01:17,792 --> 00:01:19,459
-You can shut up now, Aria.
-Well,

27
00:01:19,751 --> 00:01:22,083
I'll admit, it's impressive to
see someone survive

28
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:24,417
a fall like that with just
a bloody nose. Ha!

29
00:01:24,792 --> 00:01:26,334
Ever consider
the martial arts?

30
00:01:26,709 --> 00:01:27,876
Don't be ridiculous!

31
00:01:28,709 --> 00:01:30,834
My mind's made up.
One day I'm going to become

32
00:01:30,918 --> 00:01:33,000
a powerful magician!
I won't lose heart over

33
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:35,209
-one dumb fall.
-That's the spirit.

34
00:01:35,876 --> 00:01:38,083
No matter what,
I have to get into

35
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,959
the Royal Diana Academy
where the great

36
00:01:40,042 --> 00:01:42,626
Master Claude teaches!
My dream is to study everything

37
00:01:42,709 --> 00:01:44,792
I can about magic there
and eventually become

38
00:01:44,876 --> 00:01:47,083
a first-class magician
just like Master Claude.

39
00:01:47,167 --> 00:01:48,584
So, you best get outta my way!

40
00:01:50,709 --> 00:01:52,375
How are you going
to accomplish that

41
00:01:52,459 --> 00:01:54,584
without knowing
a single spell, huh? Hehe.

42
00:01:55,876 --> 00:01:57,876
It's no secret that
I have a lot to learn.

43
00:01:58,209 --> 00:02:00,292
That's why I do
flight training every day.

44
00:02:00,876 --> 00:02:03,542
Of course. You sure do have
weird taste though.

45
00:02:03,626 --> 00:02:05,584
-Huh?
-Most people around here

46
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:07,542
think Claude's
a bit past his prime.

47
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,209
Remember when the cultists

48
00:02:09,292 --> 00:02:11,334
attacked Diana Academy
two years ago?

49
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,792
Instead of protecting
the students,

50
00:02:14,876 --> 00:02:16,334
he just ran off like a coward.

51
00:02:17,125 --> 00:02:19,000
-[laughs]
-Would you shut up and leave me

52
00:02:19,083 --> 00:02:21,375
alone about who I look up to?
I swear I hate you!

53
00:02:21,459 --> 00:02:23,876
Come on, I'm sorry!
Don't be mad.

54
00:02:24,209 --> 00:02:26,417
If you're only here to mock me,
then back off!

55
00:02:26,626 --> 00:02:27,876
It's just that I'm concerned

56
00:02:27,959 --> 00:02:30,250
about you, that's all.
I mean, at this rate,

57
00:02:30,334 --> 00:02:32,751
-you're sure to fail.
-Uh...

58
00:02:32,834 --> 00:02:35,709
After all, the only way to learn
magic is from magicians.

59
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:37,292
Consider hiring a tutor.

60
00:02:37,751 --> 00:02:40,292
I have too many siblings
to have any extra money.

61
00:02:40,417 --> 00:02:42,626
Though I teach myself,
what else can I do?

62
00:02:42,834 --> 00:02:45,417
-[crying]
-Oh, alright, fine.

63
00:02:45,709 --> 00:02:47,459
Since we're fellow
Diana hopefuls...

64
00:02:48,083 --> 00:02:49,876
I, Aria the genius...

65
00:02:50,626 --> 00:02:53,209
will teach you Aquarius magic!

66
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:59,542
-You can leave it all to me.
-[gasps]

67
00:03:00,125 --> 00:03:02,083
We'll work out a deal where
you can pay me

68
00:03:02,167 --> 00:03:04,709
-with your body. [chuckles]
-I hope my fist will do.

69
00:03:06,959 --> 00:03:10,042
Screw Aria.
I don't need help from anybody.

70
00:03:11,584 --> 00:03:13,083
I know I can do this myself.

71
00:03:13,626 --> 00:03:16,334
I can. I can. I can!

72
00:03:17,459 --> 00:03:18,292
[screams]

73
00:03:21,584 --> 00:03:23,000
-[sharp squawk]
-[Spica grunts]

74
00:03:23,083 --> 00:03:25,083
Something just fell
from the sky, Mommy!

75
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:28,000
[FEMALE] Spica probably just
jumped off the roof again.

76
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:30,209
-[crying] Ow, why?
-<i>At this rate,</i>

77
00:03:30,292 --> 00:03:31,501
<i>you're sure to fail.</i>

78
00:03:33,542 --> 00:03:35,125
Even I know that much.

79
00:03:36,542 --> 00:03:38,459
I only have a year
before the exam,

80
00:03:38,876 --> 00:03:40,792
and I haven't made
any real progress.

81
00:03:41,375 --> 00:03:43,501
But I'm broke and I don't
have any connections

82
00:03:43,584 --> 00:03:45,834
to real magicians.
What am I gonna do?

83
00:03:46,834 --> 00:03:48,751
Good grief,
could you keep it down?

84
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,334
I was sleeping like a baby.

85
00:03:50,834 --> 00:03:52,417
Take your fascination
with suicide

86
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:54,417
somewhere else,
you foolish girl.

87
00:03:55,334 --> 00:03:58,459
No way! Is that little cat
talking? You're kidding!

88
00:03:58,626 --> 00:04:00,417
Did I unlock some sort
of awesome magic

89
00:04:00,501 --> 00:04:01,834
that lets me talk to animals?

90
00:04:01,918 --> 00:04:03,918
Can you really understand
what I'm saying?

91
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,375
Wait, you're a demon kitty,
aren't you?

92
00:04:09,542 --> 00:04:11,334
[CAT] Sagittarius Magic.

93
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:13,250
[screams]

94
00:04:14,542 --> 00:04:17,709
-[♪ magical music]
-[grunts]

95
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,167
Never call me
a cat monster again!

96
00:04:20,626 --> 00:04:23,375
I'll have you know that I was
formerly a human magician.

97
00:04:23,876 --> 00:04:25,751
Wow, a cat that thinks
it's a magician!

98
00:04:26,417 --> 00:04:29,209
I'm stuck in this form because
of a curse, but rest assured,

99
00:04:29,292 --> 00:04:30,918
I can still use some magic.

100
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:32,417
-[sighs]
-Master!

101
00:04:33,459 --> 00:04:35,876
-Please let me call you Master!
-Wait, what?!

102
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:38,876
I don't care if you're a cat,
I wanna be your apprentice!

103
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:41,334
All I'm asking is that you
please teach me magic!

104
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:44,125
I know I'm not one to talk,
but wow, you're out

105
00:04:44,209 --> 00:04:46,751
-of your mind!
-I need your help! I want to get

106
00:04:46,834 --> 00:04:49,584
-into Diana Academy.
-Do you have a clue

107
00:04:49,667 --> 00:04:52,042
what you're saying?
It's the highest-level

108
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,834
magic academy there is.

109
00:04:54,209 --> 00:04:56,042
I know that! That's why
I'm on my knees

110
00:04:56,125 --> 00:04:58,000
-begging for help!
-[grunts] No way.

111
00:04:58,334 --> 00:05:00,542
-Nothing in it for me.
-I don't have much money,

112
00:05:00,626 --> 00:05:02,292
but I'll do anything
within my power

113
00:05:02,375 --> 00:05:05,584
-to make it worth it to you!
-Anything, you say?

114
00:05:05,876 --> 00:05:06,709
[gasps]

115
00:05:07,375 --> 00:05:09,167
[voice trembling] Um, well,

116
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:11,042
if you want me to
pay with my body...

117
00:05:11,334 --> 00:05:13,501
it'd be super embarrassing,
but I suppose

118
00:05:13,584 --> 00:05:15,250
-I could at least try.
-No!

119
00:05:15,959 --> 00:05:18,792
<i>She understands me and</i>
<i>she'll do anything I want.</i>

120
00:05:19,375 --> 00:05:21,667
<i>I'd be a fool to waste</i>
<i>this opportunity.</i>

121
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:23,542
-Okay.
-[gasps]

122
00:05:24,501 --> 00:05:26,667
I can't just stand by and
ignore the needy.

123
00:05:28,292 --> 00:05:29,918
You're a total lifesaver!
Thank you

124
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,375
with every fiber of my being!

125
00:05:31,459 --> 00:05:33,083
-My name's Spica Virgo--
-[grunts]

126
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:37,000
The pleasure's all mine.
Shall we head to the capital and

127
00:05:37,083 --> 00:05:39,709
-start training?
-[gasps] Perfect!

128
00:05:40,834 --> 00:05:42,584
[♪ lively music]

129
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:47,000
Well, this is the capital.
So do you want

130
00:05:47,083 --> 00:05:49,334
-to train right here?
-Let's see.

131
00:05:49,626 --> 00:05:51,667
Raise your right hand
and chant the spell!

132
00:05:51,959 --> 00:05:54,918
-Gimia Kholdbier!
-Right!

133
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:57,918
Gimia Kholdbier!

134
00:05:58,626 --> 00:06:01,083
Sure thing, doll.
I'll bring you a pint.

135
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:02,709
Just 300 gold. Deal?

136
00:06:03,417 --> 00:06:04,751
-Huh?
-[cash register dings]

137
00:06:08,083 --> 00:06:11,459
[laughs] It's been forever
since I had a nice beer.

138
00:06:11,751 --> 00:06:14,250
[laughs] Hello there, ladies.

139
00:06:14,459 --> 00:06:17,459
-Would you care to join us?
-Look at that cute little kitty.

140
00:06:17,542 --> 00:06:20,167
[meowing loudly]

141
00:06:20,667 --> 00:06:21,542
Tell the truth.

142
00:06:22,834 --> 00:06:25,334
Are you serious about teaching
me magic or not?

143
00:06:25,417 --> 00:06:27,584
-Yes, I am.
-Also, I'm way too broke

144
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:29,542
to pay for your beer,
so that's on you!

145
00:06:29,667 --> 00:06:32,083
Yes, ma'am! Allow me
to show off some tricks.

146
00:06:32,501 --> 00:06:34,709
[coughs]

147
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:37,083
<i>When Master invited</i>
<i>that lady for a drink,</i>

148
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:39,459
<i>she talked about him like</i>
<i>he was a normal cat.</i>

149
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,125
<i>Am I really the only one</i>

150
00:06:41,209 --> 00:06:43,042
<i>who's able to hear him</i>
<i>when he speaks?</i>

151
00:06:43,709 --> 00:06:45,918
<i>Man, this girl seems</i>
<i>like bad news.</i>

152
00:06:46,250 --> 00:06:48,626
<i>I've had enough fun with her.</i>
<i>I'll just make her do</i>

153
00:06:48,709 --> 00:06:50,542
<i>something so</i>
<i>ridiculous she gives up.</i>

154
00:06:50,792 --> 00:06:52,792
Hey, I got a real
request for ya.

155
00:06:53,292 --> 00:06:54,667
-Huh?
-Master this chant before

156
00:06:54,751 --> 00:06:57,209
training, and I'll teach you
all the world's magic.

157
00:06:59,042 --> 00:07:00,375
[CAT] The Royal Library.

158
00:07:00,834 --> 00:07:02,542
Anything you could
imagine is here.

159
00:07:02,959 --> 00:07:04,792
From picture books
to magic tomes.

160
00:07:05,459 --> 00:07:08,709
Including a legendary grimoire
that's very hard to find.

161
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:11,751
One that imparts great wisdom
to whoever holds it.

162
00:07:12,626 --> 00:07:14,334
The Book of Providence.

163
00:07:14,792 --> 00:07:16,000
Protestants?

164
00:07:16,417 --> 00:07:19,000
No, more like "Providence,"
as in the ability

165
00:07:19,083 --> 00:07:21,292
to see everything,
like omniscience.

166
00:07:21,834 --> 00:07:24,125
I want you to read it
and learn how to release me

167
00:07:24,209 --> 00:07:27,083
from this wretched curse.
That's my request.

168
00:07:27,584 --> 00:07:29,250
So where is this special book?

169
00:07:29,459 --> 00:07:31,125
I'm asking you
cause I don't know.

170
00:07:31,709 --> 00:07:33,417
Well, you should
get to it eventually

171
00:07:33,501 --> 00:07:35,209
if you go through
all the grimoires.

172
00:07:35,709 --> 00:07:37,709
But there's like
100,000 books in here!

173
00:07:37,918 --> 00:07:40,501
Let's see.
I'll give you about a month.

174
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:42,417
You aren't even listening!

175
00:07:42,792 --> 00:07:45,709
At the very least, I hope you
plan on helping me look for it.

176
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,918
[CAT] I'd love to look for
it myself, but... [grunts]

177
00:07:49,083 --> 00:07:52,000
things get complicated when a
non-human tries to take a book.

178
00:07:52,083 --> 00:07:54,167
[loud alarm blaring]

179
00:07:55,042 --> 00:07:57,375
The Mother Book overseeing
the library detects it

180
00:07:57,459 --> 00:08:00,209
and sounds the alarm,
and the guard shows up.

181
00:08:00,667 --> 00:08:03,334
I won't let that filthy cat
get away this time!

182
00:08:03,542 --> 00:08:05,250
There you have it.
Well, good luck.

183
00:08:05,334 --> 00:08:07,626
There's no way I'll find it on
my own, you know.

184
00:08:07,709 --> 00:08:09,709
Forget about being
my apprentice then.

185
00:08:10,459 --> 00:08:13,250
[grunts] Fine, I got this.

186
00:08:13,667 --> 00:08:16,375
-I'll show you! Bring it on!
-Get back here, damn cat!

187
00:08:17,626 --> 00:08:20,417
She'll be lucky to find it
in a year, let alone a month.

188
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:23,626
An apprentice is a pain
in the rear I do not need.

189
00:08:24,167 --> 00:08:25,250
Nothing personal.

190
00:08:33,042 --> 00:08:34,250
-[Spica yells]
-[screams]

191
00:08:36,918 --> 00:08:38,083
[meows]

192
00:08:40,209 --> 00:08:42,042
I read a book about
transformation magic

193
00:08:42,125 --> 00:08:43,834
and got turned into a cat too.

194
00:08:44,125 --> 00:08:46,667
-Now what am I supposed to do?
-Yoo-hoo!

195
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,959
You must be careful.
Some books have magic

196
00:08:49,042 --> 00:08:50,709
that activates
when you open them.

197
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:52,250
You coulda warned me!

198
00:08:54,751 --> 00:08:56,501
[screams]

199
00:08:57,876 --> 00:08:59,626
[breathes deeply]

200
00:09:01,751 --> 00:09:03,918
[MALE] Let's learn
about anatomy together!

201
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,417
[shrieks]

202
00:09:05,792 --> 00:09:07,834
I didn't know
grimoires were so scary.

203
00:09:08,417 --> 00:09:10,209
That's enough for today.

204
00:09:11,042 --> 00:09:13,375
<i>I give her three days, tops.</i>

205
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,959
-[NARRATOR] <i>However...</i>
-[♪ lively music]

206
00:09:30,709 --> 00:09:32,584
<i>The daunting task did not deter</i>

207
00:09:32,667 --> 00:09:34,667
<i>Spica from continuing</i>
<i>her search.</i>

208
00:09:39,751 --> 00:09:41,167
[CAT] Whatcha doin'?

209
00:09:41,375 --> 00:09:43,083
I'm studying
these ancient runes.

210
00:09:43,459 --> 00:09:46,209
Are you now? What happened
to looking for the book?

211
00:09:46,918 --> 00:09:49,209
I remembered that you said
the Book of Providence

212
00:09:49,292 --> 00:09:50,459
is a legendary grimoire.

213
00:09:51,083 --> 00:09:52,834
That made me think
it might be written

214
00:09:52,918 --> 00:09:55,417
in an ancient language.
So, I figured it wouldn't hurt

215
00:09:55,501 --> 00:09:58,876
-to research some.
-Oh. What a clever insight.

216
00:09:59,876 --> 00:10:02,167
I never expected you
to be so studious.

217
00:10:02,375 --> 00:10:04,751
Well, I never was before.
I mean,

218
00:10:04,834 --> 00:10:06,167
I don't even like to read.

219
00:10:06,834 --> 00:10:09,751
But the more of this I read,
the more interested I became.

220
00:10:10,167 --> 00:10:11,834
And now I want
to learn all I can.

221
00:10:13,083 --> 00:10:15,501
It says here that carving
the runes is what actually

222
00:10:15,584 --> 00:10:17,125
-activates their magic.
-[sighs]

223
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,042
It appears as though
I underestimated you.

224
00:10:21,375 --> 00:10:23,000
-Hmm.
-But unfortunately...

225
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:25,501
-[bell tolling]
-that's the closing bell.

226
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,792
-You're out of time.
-Huh?

227
00:10:28,626 --> 00:10:31,667
-Today's the one-month cutoff.
-No way! That's not fair!

228
00:10:31,751 --> 00:10:33,542
Can't you give me
a little more time?

229
00:10:34,167 --> 00:10:35,959
-It won't make a difference.
-[gasps]

230
00:10:36,083 --> 00:10:39,709
Please don't go! All I want is
to get into Diana Academy!

231
00:10:40,918 --> 00:10:42,959
Why are you so fixated on Diana?

232
00:10:43,417 --> 00:10:45,292
What's there that
you want so badly?

233
00:10:46,918 --> 00:10:49,792
They can help me achieve
my dream to be a first-class

234
00:10:49,876 --> 00:10:52,292
-magician like Master Claude.
-Claude?

235
00:10:53,209 --> 00:10:55,125
Even though everyone says
he's a coward?

236
00:10:55,292 --> 00:10:56,751
Who cares what people say?

237
00:10:56,876 --> 00:10:58,667
[♪ sentimental music]

238
